Sign Se Pehle (साइन से पहले) is a voice-first tool that helps people understand a rental agreement before they sign it.

The problem: Most people sign rental agreements they can’t fully read, often written in dense legal English or a mix of languages. They miss things like lock-in penalties, deposit forfeiture, and one-sided notice rules.

What it does:

You upload a photo or PDF of the agreement.
Sarvam Vision reads the text, even from a messy photo.
Sarvam-105B finds the riskiest clauses, marks each red, amber, or green, and shows the exact line from the contract.
It explains each clause in plain words in your language (Hindi, Telugu, Tamil, and more).
Bulbul reads the explanation aloud.
You can ask “What if I leave after 4 months?” and it answers from your own contract.

Why it matters: It helps first-time tenants, students, and migrants who can’t read legal text, and it works in Indian languages, so it’s accessible to people who aren’t comfortable in English.

Limit: It’s not legal advice. It points out clauses worth questioning.

One-line pitch: “Photograph your rental agreement, see the risky clauses with the exact line, and hear them explained in your own language before you sign.”
